G5.3b.7 entry design:

- This phase assembles one production-shaped topology behind isolated
  constructors. It does not start that topology from `TxPoolServiceBuilder`,
  mutate a legacy `TxPool`/`PrePool`/`EffectJournal`, or create a shadow read or
  write path. G5.3c remains the single ownership switch.
- The exact long-lived tasks are the set in section 11. Their capabilities are
  closed: resolver and verifier workers own checked-out compute leases; Ready
  and maintenance own only level reads and total Plan/Apply calls; the ordered
  chain handler owns one retained chain command at a time; the publisher owns
  the sole effect lease; cache and block-assembler tasks own only derived
  endpoints. The dispatcher owns bounded request execution, never membership.
- One shared transient compute-execution gate is compiled from the same checked
  `N + 1` formula that sizes the authority compute partition. Retained workers
  acquire a permit before checkout and keep it through settlement or typed
  staleness. Local and TestAccept acquire the same permit before direct capture
  and keep it through verification and final settlement/evaluation. Waiting for
  a permit owns no authority capability and holds no guard. Ready, maintenance,
  chain planning, template construction and block validation do not consume
  this tx-pool VM permit. The gate is execution capacity only and cannot decide
  transaction location, charge, ordering or admission.
- Verification-cache evidence is bound constructively. A prepared retained or
  direct verification request is consumed by an exact lookup against
  `TxVerificationCache`; the lookup returns a move-only cache-bound request and
  only that type exposes execution. No API accepts an independently obtained
  `Option<Completed>`, and no caller can pair the cached result for request A
  with request B. The existing fixed-size witness hash plus exact
  `ScriptVerificationRules` remains the sole key.
- The maintenance driver owns no queue, cursor, population mirror or retry
  ledger. It subscribes before reading authority levels, performs a bounded
  fair round over Remote expiry, one Accepted root/closure, and dependency dirty
  work, and uses a timer only for wall-clock due work. Progress repeats through
  bounded steps with cooperative yield; an idle read waits on level hints or the
  next expiry tick. Legal resource pressure is typed backoff, not fail-stop.
- The block assembler keeps its established concurrency domains. Full and reset
  remain ordered only at the short publication boundary; their construction
  overlaps proposal, transaction and uncle partial construction. Full ignores
  partial revisions and retains priority, reset epoch-fences stale full work,
  and partial receipts use optimistic revisions and may be skipped. Candidate
  uncles stay under their existing short bounded lock and production mutation
  uses typed `try_insert`; no full/reset/partial actor or authority lock is
  introduced.
- Startup removes the cause of the legacy zombie protocol. The ordered reorg
  sender exists before service tasks start and never drops a chain delta merely
  because ordinary ingress is closed. Persistence re-enters ordinary validation
  against the initial paired snapshot; queued exact chain updates then advance
  that same authority/snapshot pair in order. Ordinary controller ingress opens
  only after replay and catch-up. `onchain_reconcile_done`, the first-later-block
  database scan and any replacement marker or repair scan are deleted at
  G5.3c.
- Shutdown is a capability drain, not panic recovery: close ordinary ingress
  and the chain/admin producer boundary; concurrently cancel compute, Ready and
  maintenance and open the shutdown-only relay circuit; leave the sole
  publisher alive so effect capacity can release every pending settlement;
  join producers; close the effect producer; drain and join the publisher;
  capture persistence after the drain; then stop derived services. A
  structural task fault requests this controlled sequence. Legal hostile
  input, stale work, endpoint failure, backpressure and resource exhaustion
  remain typed outcomes.

